IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cc-dates`
IMPORT `cc-rules`
IMPORT `cc-seat`

-- County Court Act 1958 (Vic) -- worked cases for the party's questions (cc-seat.l4), the s 72(3) rule and the date helpers.
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output.
-- Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The facts are illustrative.
-- Breached traces are asserted with CONSIDER ... WHEN FULFILLED (EVALTRACE ... EQUALS cannot test a breach).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`

GIVEN `the time` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the defendant's notice is in time at day` `the time` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `s 72(3) -- the defendant's jury notice within four days` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the defendant` `give notice in writing requiring a jury` `the time`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `Dates`

-- 1 January to 15 March 2027: 31 + 28 + 14 = 73 days; 2028 is a leap year (366 days).
#ASSERT `the days from` (`d` 1 1 2027) `to` (`d` 15 3 2027) EQUALS 73
#ASSERT `the days from` (`d` 1 1 2028) `to` (`d` 1 1 2029) EQUALS 366
#ASSERT `the date` 4 `days after` (`d` 10 3 2027) EQUALS `d` 14 3 2027
#ASSERT `the date` 4 `days after` (`d` 27 2 2028) EQUALS `d` 2 3 2028

§§ `ss 36, 37 -- can the County Court hear my claim`

-- Arguments: kind, excluded by another Act, where it arose, defendant resided in Victoria when served.
#ASSERT `Can the County Court hear my claim` `a claim of any other kind` FALSE `wholly within Victoria` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the County Court hear my claim` `a claim of any other kind` FALSE `wholly within Victoria` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the County Court hear my claim` `a claim of any other kind` TRUE `wholly within Victoria` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can the County Court hear my claim` `a claim against a municipal council for an accident on a road or other place it controls` TRUE `wholly within Victoria` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the County Court hear my claim` `a proceeding another Act gives the County Court jurisdiction over` FALSE `wholly within Victoria` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the County Court hear my claim` `an application for a prerogative writ or an order in the nature of one` FALSE `wholly within Victoria` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the County Court hear my claim` `a proceeding brought upon a judgment of the Supreme Court` FALSE `wholly within Victoria` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the County Court hear my claim` `a claim of any other kind` FALSE `partly outside Victoria, with a material part within Victoria` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the County Court hear my claim` `a claim of any other kind` FALSE `partly outside Victoria, with no material part within Victoria` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can the County Court hear my claim` `a claim of any other kind` FALSE `partly outside Victoria, with no material part within Victoria` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the County Court hear my claim` `a claim of any other kind` FALSE `wholly outside Victoria` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the County Court hear my claim` `a claim of any other kind` FALSE `wholly outside Victoria` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A no from either section wins over a not-answered from the other.
#ASSERT `Can the County Court hear my claim` `a claim of any other kind` TRUE `wholly outside Victoria` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the County Court hear my claim` `an application for a prerogative writ or an order in the nature of one` FALSE `partly outside Victoria, with no material part within Victoria` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 39(2), 55 -- a proceeding beyond jurisdiction; s 51 -- counter-claims`

#ASSERT `What happens if my claim is outside the Court's jurisdiction` `within jurisdiction` FALSE EQUALS `nothing: the proceeding is within jurisdiction`
#ASSERT `What happens if my claim is outside the Court's jurisdiction` `partly beyond jurisdiction` FALSE EQUALS `the Court may amend it, stay it for a transfer application, or strike it out with costs as if it were dismissed (s 39(2))`
#ASSERT `What happens if my claim is outside the Court's jurisdiction` `partly beyond jurisdiction` TRUE EQUALS `the Court may amend it, stay it for a transfer application, or strike it out with costs as if it were dismissed (s 39(2))`
#ASSERT `What happens if my claim is outside the Court's jurisdiction` `wholly beyond jurisdiction` TRUE EQUALS `it may go on with the parties' consent to the Court having jurisdiction (s 55)`
#ASSERT `What happens if my claim is outside the Court's jurisdiction` `wholly beyond jurisdiction` FALSE EQUALS `it must be struck out with costs as if the plaintiff failed, unless the Court first amends it or stays it for a transfer (ss 55, 39(2))`

#ASSERT `Can the counter-claim get relief beyond jurisdiction` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the counter-claim get relief beyond jurisdiction` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the counter-claim get relief beyond jurisdiction` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

