§§ `ss 39B, 39C -- where money for a child or person under disability goes`

-- Arguments: minor, cannot manage, ordered otherwise (s 39B), ordered otherwise (s 39C). For a minor both sections speak
-- (finding 3).
#ASSERT `Where does the money awarded go` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS LIST `into the County Court, then out to an administrator the Court specifies (s 39B(1))`, `into the Supreme Court, to the Senior Master, to be held for the person (s 39C(3))`
#ASSERT `Where does the money awarded go` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS LIST `into the County Court, then as the Court otherwise orders (s 39B(1))`, `into the Supreme Court, to the Senior Master, to be held for the person (s 39C(3))`
#ASSERT `Where does the money awarded go` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS LIST `into the County Court, then out to an administrator the Court specifies (s 39B(1))`, `as the Court orders otherwise than into the Supreme Court (s 39C(3))`
#ASSERT `Where does the money awarded go` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS LIST `into the Supreme Court, to the Senior Master, to be held for the person (s 39C(3))`
#ASSERT `Where does the money awarded go` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS LIST `as the Court orders otherwise than into the Supreme Court (s 39C(3))`
#ASSERT `Where does the money awarded go` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS EMPTY

§§ `ss 46, 47, 47A, 47B -- arbitration and mediation`

#ASSERT `Can the mediation be used as evidence` `a mediation the Court referred the proceeding to` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the mediation be used as evidence` `a mediation the Court referred the proceeding to` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the mediation be used as evidence` `a judicial resolution conference` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can the mediation be used as evidence` `a mediation the Court did not refer` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `Can the arbitration award be challenged` `the parties agreed and the Court referred it to arbitrators they named (s 46)` EQUALS `binding, final and conclusive unless set aside; the Court may set it aside or refer it back on an application at the first sitting after one week from its entry (s 46(2), (4))`
#ASSERT `Can the arbitration award be challenged` `the parties agreed in writing and the Court acted as arbitrator (s 47)` EQUALS `not open to question or appeal in any court (s 47)`
#ASSERT `Can the arbitration award be challenged` `the Court referred it under s 47A` EQUALS `not answered here: the rules and the Civil Procedure Act 2010 govern (s 47A)`

