§§ `s 37(3) -- recovering more than was claimed`

-- Arguments: verdict, amount sought, percentage reduction.
#ASSERT `Can I recover more than I claimed` 600000 500000 0 EQUALS JUST 600000
-- 600000 less 25% = 450000: the reduced amount, here below the amount sought.
#ASSERT `Can I recover more than I claimed` 600000 500000 25 EQUALS JUST 450000
-- 800000 less 10% = 720000, above the 500000 sought.
#ASSERT `Can I recover more than I claimed` 800000 500000 10 EQUALS JUST 720000
#ASSERT `Can I recover more than I claimed` 500001 500000 0 EQUALS JUST 500001
#ASSERT `Can I recover more than I claimed` 500000 500000 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I recover more than I claimed` 300000 500000 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 73(4) -- interest on the judgment debt`

-- Arguments: debt, rate percent a year, from, to. Interest = debt x rate/100 x days/365.
-- 100000 at 10% for 73 days (1 Jan to 15 Mar 2027): 100000 x 0.10 x 73/365 = 2000.
#ASSERT `How much interest does my judgment carry` 100000 10 (`d` 1 1 2027) (`d` 15 3 2027) EQUALS 2000
-- A whole non-leap year: 10000.
#ASSERT `How much interest does my judgment carry` 100000 10 (`d` 1 1 2027) (`d` 1 1 2028) EQUALS 10000
-- A leap year has 366 days: 36500 x 0.10 x 366/365 = 3660 (fork F7).
#ASSERT `How much interest does my judgment carry` 36500 10 (`d` 1 1 2028) (`d` 1 1 2029) EQUALS 3660
-- One day: 36500 x 0.10 / 365 = 10.
#ASSERT `How much interest does my judgment carry` 36500 10 (`d` 31 12 2027) (`d` 1 1 2028) EQUALS 10
-- The same day, and a day before the start: none.
#ASSERT `How much interest does my judgment carry` 100000 10 (`d` 1 1 2027) (`d` 1 1 2027) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `How much interest does my judgment carry` 100000 10 (`d` 1 1 2027) (`d` 31 12 2026) EQUALS 0

